# VSC-353 closure check (author: t353-check-author-2, not the fixer). RED until the stale-figures class (A) reports the "<n> declared/<n> owned" shapes without the two false-positive families AND (B) reports a MISMATCH finding naming both figures when a current-tense "<n> declared" disagrees with the number of paths .gitmodules declares, while (C) equal counts and (D) historical-marked lines are not reported as a mismatch. 'owned' has no honest source of truth in a bare repo, so no owned-mismatch clause exists.
